        "context": "section",
        "id": "_syntax",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Syntax"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "By default, the subject (i.e., the term) is followed immediately by a colon (still in bold) and offset from the description by a space. You can replace the colon with another character (or sequence of characters) using the block attribute named "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "subject-stop"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "[unordered,subject-stop=)]\nalpha:: partially feature complete, unstable, and subject to change\nbeta:: feature complete and undergoing testing"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Here’s how this syntax will appear, where supported:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "ulist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "blocks": [],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "alpha)"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "strong",
                        "roles": []
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": " partially feature complete, unstable, and subject to change"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "blocks": [],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "beta)"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "strong",
                        "roles": []
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": " feature complete and undergoing testing"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "style": null,
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If the term ends with a period or the value of the subject-stop attribute, the subject stop is not added."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To insert a space between the subject and visible stop character(s), add a space character at the start of the value of the subject-stop attribute. You’ll also need to enclose the value in double quotes so the space character is preserved."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "tip"
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "_subject_stop",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Subject stop"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "A description list with marker uses a run-in layout by default. In other words, the subject appears on the same line as the description, separated by the subject stop and a space. To make the subject appear above the description, like in a normal description list, add the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "stack"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " role to the list. In this case, the stop character is only added if specified explicitly."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "[unordered.stack]\nboolean:: use true and false, not 1 and 0 or T and F\nnumber:: use Arabic numerals without punctuation (other than the decimal point to make a floating point number)\nenumerated value:: use only one of the allowed values, respecting case"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Here’s how this syntax will appear, where supported:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "ulist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "blocks": [],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "boolean"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "strong",
                        "roles": []
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "line-break"
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": " use true and false, not 1 and 0 or T and F"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "blocks": [],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "number"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "strong",
                        "roles": []
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "line-break"
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": " use Arabic numerals without punctuation (other than the decimal point in a floating point number)"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "blocks": [],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "enumerated value"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "strong",
                        "roles": []
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "line-break"
                      },
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": " use only one of the allowed values, respecting case"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "style": null,
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "We may decide to replace the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "stack"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " role with the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "stacked"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " option (i.e., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "%stacked"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). Alternately, we may decide to reverse the default behavior and make a description list with marker stacked by default, with "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "run-in"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " as an option (i.e., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "%run-in"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). These adjustments will be made when this feature is standardized."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "warning"
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "_stacked",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Stacked"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "As an alternative to using a description list with marker, you can use a normal unordered or ordered list and format the subject and stop character manually."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "* *boolean:* use true and false, not 1 and 0 or T and F\n* *number:* use Arabic numerals without punctuation (other than the decimal point in a floating point number)\n* *enumerated value:* use only one of the allowed values, respecting case"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "This syntax gives you maximum portability in the short-term."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Although lacking proper semantics, the other way to achieve the same result is to nest a single-item description list inside an otherwise empty list item."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "* {empty}\nboolean:: use true and false, not 1 and 0 or T and F\n* {empty}\nnumber:: use Arabic numerals without punctuation (other than the decimal point in a floating point number)\n* {empty}\nenumerated value:: use only one of the allowed values, respecting case"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "_alternatives",
        "level": 1,
